ext{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{p+(-p)}{2},\\frac{-3q+7q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{4q}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,2q)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19156b0d-85dd-55bf-92c5-90b05ca8405a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19156b0d-85dd-55bf-92c5-90b05ca8405a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232317} :answer-field/id #uuid "664dfe98-66e6-5bae-a9a7-b47a5a5e45f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d59528-68c8-562f-b103-349c4f60afa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d59528-68c8-562f-b103-349c4f60afa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232319} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a16269-c3d6-50fd-9b87-ae55cd7d3020" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f0c1db7-3670-5389-b242-c12c078528a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-216929" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(4a,-2b)$ and $(-2a,2b)$ is$\\,($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(4a,-2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-2a,2b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4a+(-2a)}{2},\\frac{-2b+2b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2a}{2},\\frac{0}{2}) \\\\  & =(a,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
